  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x6BCE" flags="0x0">
    <title>DFCO Full Restore RPM Threshold</title>
    <description>Exact 1EK7A. Address 0x14488; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Coolant-indexed lower/full-restore RPM threshold in FUN 00050018. At speed count below 4 it is the lower boundary for class 3. At speed count 4 or above every branch reachable under the stock compile-time flags returns class 3 at or below the effective lower threshold and class 0 only strictly above it. The adjusted result is stored in ffff16aa after coolant floors, runtime offsets, and a conditional minimum of 48 counts or 1200 RPM. Exact stock moving branches ignore upper/intermediate table 0001298c. The target-vehicle capture selected only moving samples, retained stock 000126e4/00012718, changed both restore tables, and eliminated the full 0x3f inhibit mask below 5000 RPM. Because 0001298c is not compared on that branch, this hardware result isolates 00012818 as the operational moving veto. Equality remains class 3, so a raw value of 200 vetoes through exactly 5000 RPM in the quantized coordinate and class 0 begins only above it. Result disposition: inline_comparison. Definition address projected from JK08A 00012818 through JK08A-1EK7A.definition-addresses.csv: The target operand 00014488 at site 0007db22 corresponds to the 1ME3B definition operand 00014008. Static diagnostic context: Engine Coolant Temperature [code, homologous_community, via map evidence: indexed_by].</description>
