  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xC469" flags="0x0">
    <title>MAF Factor</title>
    <description>Exact 1EK7A. Address 0x89D1; 1 rows x 1 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Fixed-address unsigned MAF Factor byte in the 7mfk primary BFS calculation. ROM8[0x8a27]=109 multiplies positive signed-tested aggregate Q and ROM16 K; after /256 the stock split product retains low 40 bits before unsigned speed division. The aggregate is not an index. Stock F is 109. The A2L MAF Factor entry matches the byte's operational position, representation, and cross-ROM literal-pool signature and distinguishes it from K-Value. Homologous values are 133 for 1ND0A/1ND3B, 131 for JK78C, 109 for JK03A/JK08A, and 132 for JK00D. The engineering unit and multiplier remain source-derived pending hardware validation. J1979 Mode 01 PID 0x10 declares ROM8[0x83ec]/25600 g/s per count of the total quantity that the Base Fuel Schedule producer reproduces from A+B, which is 0.01477 kg/hr per count with stock 105, while F*0.0001 gives 0.0109 kg/hr per count; the A2L unit of F does not match the ECU's declared airflow. Definition address projected from JK08A 00008a27 through JK08A-1EK7A.definition-addresses.csv: The target operand 000089d1 at site 0004967e corresponds to the 1ME3B definition operand 00008965.</description>
