  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0xA7EE" flags="0x0">
    <title>Stationary Engine Speed Limit</title>
    <description>Exact 1EK7A. Address 0x8567; 1 rows x 2 columns; uint8; map confidence code. Stationary rev-limiter fuel-cut/restore hysteresis. Entry requires coarse vehicle speed ffff110e to equal zero. With readiness bit 4 of ffff247f set and state bit 5 clear, engine speed ffff11ae reaching cell 0 sets fuel cut. While bit 5 is set, speed below cell 1 restores fueling. FUN 0004ed88 includes the Boolean result in the aggregate fuel-output inhibit path. The stored bytes are 36 and 30, or 1800 and 1500 RPM. Readiness requires accumulator ffff16a6 to reach ROM16[0000911c]. Exact firmware traces CAN 0x284 vehicle speed through ffff113c, ffff115e, ffff118e, and the scheduler snapshot ffff110e; the required zero value establishes the stationary role. Additional entry gates ffff244f bit 2 and ffff2458 bit 5 remain physically unnamed. Definition address projected from JK08A 000085d9 through JK08A-1EK7A.definition-addresses.csv: The target operand 00008567 at site 0007ca9c corresponds to the 1ME3B definition operand 00008538. Static diagnostic context: ENG SPEED [code, homologous_vq35hr, via map evidence: indexed_by].</description>
