    <description>Exact 1EK7A. Address 0x16AFC; 1 rows x 8 columns; uint16; map confidence code. RPM-indexed unsigned coefficient for a bounded engine-torque correction. FUN 000658a4 multiplies the interpolated value by a nonnegative byte difference, divides by 256, and writes the result to ffff14e2 for the downstream torque-state arithmetic. The direct scratch copy ffff14e4 has no external reader, but the same live lookup result remains in r6 and is consumed at 00065908 before ffff14e2 is written. FUN 00065cd8 and FUN 00064a1c add or subtract ffff14e2 in the same raw domain as offset-binary Engine Torque Map 00010b8e. The continuous consumer path assigns an engine-torque correction role. The physical x*0.1 Nm conversion follows the Engine Torque Map catalog and requires hardware validation. Result disposition: consumer. Definition address projected from JK08A 00014c1a through JK08A-1EK7A.definition-addresses.csv: The target operand 00016afc at site 0009bbfe corresponds to the 1ME3B definition operand 000163b4.</description>
